ok - a silent supervision chain becomes one durable wake, one episode record, and an active alert
ok - an open episode appends one wake and alerts once per interval, not once per tick
ok - away mode keeps the deadman inert, so only one process ever injects into the pane
ok - ordinary Stop-owned recovery already under way keeps the deadman out of the way
ok - a live identity-matched watcher with a fresh beat is healthy and never alarms
ok - a home with nothing in flight is not an outage
ok - a delivered rewake that no turn ever handled is a trigger on its own, even behind a live watcher
ok - self-recovery sends exactly one turn-end-guard input into firstmate's pane per backoff window
ok - an unconfirmed submit is recorded and still spends its backoff window rather than retyping
ok - self-recovery defers to a running turn and keeps the open episode's record
ok - a six-minute handling turn with the pane mid-turn is not an outage
ok - an idle pane after a dead rewake turn still alarms, records, and self-recovers
ok - self-recovery refuses any pane whose composer is not positively proven empty
ok - recovery closes the episode and stops the injections
ok - ensure starts exactly one deadman, detached from its starter's process group, and stop retires it
ok - a real arm starts this home's deadman outside its own process group and a later arm keeps the same one
ok - the deadman retires itself when the session that owned its home is gone
ok - a deadman retires when a different session takes over its home, so the next arm starts one from that session
ok - ensure resolves firstmate's harness from its own ancestry and hands it to the detached deadman, so a mid-turn pane still reads busy there
ok - ensure retires a deadman started under a superseded session and starts one for the current session at once
ok - stop lands immediately even when the deadman is deep inside a production-length tick, and releases its lock completely
ok - a linked task worktree never starts a deadman
ok - a handling turn's drain retires the delivered-rewake marker
ok - the first alarm fires on the tick that opens the episode, and a future-dated stamp never suppresses an alarm
ok - the alarm reaches the captain whether injection is deferred by unsent text or by a turn busy past its bound
ok - consecutive unsent-text deferrals alarm in plain words at the threshold, repeat on the interval, and never touch the text
ok - a window with no readable input box escalates as its own plain-words cause
ok - stopping the deadman terminates a notifier it was still running, as the away-mode daemon does
